#################################################################
#  LSPU-LB MERGED ONTOLOGY
#  Combines three pillars into one Turtle file so the RAG app's
#  single-ontology loader (OntologyStore) can query all of them:
#    - Pillar 1: Program Information   (namespace: lspuprog:)
#      source: pillar1_program_ontology.ttl (REVISED — see below)
#    - Pillar 3: Student Life & Conduct Policy / Handbook (namespace: lspu:)
#      source: pillar3_handbook_ontology.ttl
#    - Pillar 2: Admission & Transaction Procedures / Citizen's
#      Charter (namespace: lspuadm:)
#      source: LSPU_Citizens_Charter_2026_CLEANED.txt (2026, 1st Edition)
#  No URI/prefix collisions between the source files: each pillar
#  uses its own namespace, so this is mostly a straight concatenation.
#  Pillar 2 additionally CROSS-REFERENCES classes/properties/
#  instances already defined under lspu: (lspu:Office, lspu:Document,
#  lspu:requiresDocument, lspu:hasStep, lspu:nextStep, lspu:performedBy,
#  lspu:UniversityRole, lspu:definition) instead of duplicating them,
#  and REUSES the four office instances Pillar 3 already created
#  (lspu:OfficeOfTheRegistrar, lspu:OSAS, lspu:GuidanceOffice,
#  lspu:SafetyAndSecurityManagementOffice) rather than redefining them.
#
#  STATUS OF PILLAR 1 (replaced in this batch):
#  - Course-level curricula and unit loads (Course, CourseOffering,
#    CourseCategory, YearLevel, Semester) have been REMOVED, since
#    only 3 of 23 programs ever had complete curriculum data.
#  - lspuprog:AdmissionRequirement is now POPULATED with real
#    per-program minimum general weighted average cutoffs, sourced
#    from the LSPU Admission Guidelines (1st Semester AY 2026-2027,
#    Annex A) — NOT from the Citizen's Charter. Pillar 2's
#    lspuadm:feedsAdmissionRequirement still points at the
#    lspuprog:AdmissionRequirement CLASS (the Charter only describes
#    the entrance-exam PROCESS, not per-program numeric cutoffs);
#    the real per-program cutoff INSTANCES (lspuprog:AdmReq_*) now
#    live entirely within Pillar 1.
#  - Bachelor of Physical Education admission cutoff was not supplied
#    by the user and is flagged accordingly within Pillar 1 itself.
#
#  STATUS OF PILLAR 2 (as of this batch):
#  - FULLY POPULATED with complete client-step / agency-action / fee /
#    processing-time / person-responsible chains, each step carrying
#    its own page-level source citation: ALL of Section A -- Frontline
#    Services -- EXCEPT Research & Development and Extension &
#    Training Services. That is: Enrollment and Issuance of TOR/
#    Transfer Credentials/Certifications/CAV/Authenticated Documents
#    (Registrar); Collection of Fees Online basis, Releasing of Check,
#    Releasing of Cash (Cashier); Request for Refund Payment,
#    Assessment of Fees, Releasing of Clearance, Releasing of
#    Statement of Accounts (Accounting); Public Assistance w/ and w/o
#    vehicle (Security); Processing of Student ID (BAMPO); Routine
#    Medical and Dental Services (Health); Library Reference
#    Assistance, Circulation, Use of Facilities (Library); all 7 OSAS
#    services (clearances, student-org recognition, ID validation,
#    3 Good Moral Certificate variants); Processing of Scholarship and
#    Financial Assistance; and LSPU Entrance Examination + Appraisal
#    (Guidance Office). 24 services, 68 steps, all individually cited.
#  - BATCH 3 ADDED: all 9 Colleges services, Guidance Counseling, and
#    the Feedback and Complaints Mechanism.
#  - BATCH 4 ADDED: R&D services 1-6 (incl. Research Capability
#    Building and IACUC Review, previously missing), both Extension &
#    Training services (previously missing), PPMP Consolidation
#    (previously missing), and the 3 Curriculum & Instruction
#    Development services (previously missing; classified 'Academic'
#    in the Charter, a non-RA-11032 label preserved as
#    lspuadm:Cat_Academic). Two source-data quirks are flagged inline
#    with rdfs:comment (duplicated step table under 'Offering of New
#    Curricular Program'; duplicated steps 8/9 in Curriculum Review).
#    ALL of Section A (Frontline) is now fully detailed.
#  - CATALOG-LEVEL ONLY for the remaining non-frontline Section B
#    services (University President through Gender and Development,
#    Records Management, IP/technology offices, etc.): name, office,
#    classification, transaction type, who-may-avail, page citation.
#  - The LSPU Entrance Examination service is explicitly linked
#    (lspuadm:feedsAdmissionRequirement) to all 23 of Pillar 1's real
#    per-program lspuprog:AdmReq_* cutoff instances, not just to the
#    generic AdmissionRequirement class.
#
#  PROVENANCE / CITATION COVERAGE (so a RAG answer can say "based on
#  the Student Handbook, Ch. X" or "based on the Citizen's Charter,
#  Office of Y, Step Z"):
#  - Pillar 1: lspuprog:sourceDocument on Programs/CMOs/admission
#    cutoffs — points to the governing CMO or the Admission Guidelines.
#  - Pillar 3: lspu:sourceArticle on policy-bearing instances (offenses,
#    sanctions, rights, duties, procedures) — points to the Handbook's
#    own Chapter/Article/Section numbering.
#  - Pillar 2: lspuadm:sourceDocument + lspuadm:sourceSection on every
#    one of the 100 Service instances, AND on every one of the 68
#    ServiceSteps belonging to the 24 flagship services — names the
#    Charter edition and the exact office section, service, step
#    number, and page it was transcribed from (e.g. "I. Office of the
#    Registrar, Service 1: Enrollment, Step 2, p. 3"), sourced from
#    the Charter's own Table of Contents and body text.
#  Reference/supporting entities that are just linked-to metadata
#  rather than independent facts (Document, Office, UniversityRole,
#  category/transaction-type individuals) do NOT carry their own
#  separate source citation — they inherit provenance from the
#  Service/ServiceStep/Policy/Program they belong to, the same way a
#  citation for a paragraph covers the sentences inside it.
#################################################################


#################################################################
#  PILLAR 1 — PROGRAM INFORMATION (source: pillar1_program_ontology.ttl)
#################################################################

@prefix lspuprog: <http://lspu.edu.ph/ontology/program#> .
@prefix owl:      <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:      <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:      <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

#################################################################
#  LSPU-LB PROGRAM INFORMATION ONTOLOGY (Pillar 1)
#  Campus scope: LSPU Los Baños (LSPU-LB) only.
#  Companion to pillar3_handbook_ontology.ttl (Student Life &
#  Conduct). This file covers: colleges, degrees/majors/programs,
#  admission requirements (minimum general weighted average cutoffs),
#  skills typically developed, and general career/job outcomes.
#
#  STATUS OF THIS BATCH:
#  - Course-level curricula and unit loads (Course, CourseOffering,
#    CourseCategory, YearLevel, Semester) have been REMOVED at the
#    user's request, since only 3 of 23 programs ever had complete
#    curriculum data and the rest were skeleton-only. This file now
#    focuses on program identity, admission cutoffs, and general
#    program/career information.
#  - Admission requirements: minimumGeneralWeightedAverage is now
#    POPULATED for every program using the user-supplied 2026 LSPU-LB
#    minimum-grade admission requirements (not from any Pillar 2
#    document). One program (Bachelor of Physical Education) had no
#    grade requirement supplied by the user and is flagged with a
#    sourceDataGap instead of a fabricated number.
#  - programOverview, Skill, and JobOutcome individuals are populated
#    for ALL 23 programs (previously only 3). These are written from
#    general, publicly available knowledge about each field of study
#    in the Philippine CHED context (typical for the degree type, not
#    LSPU-specific claims) rather than any official LSPU curriculum
#    document, and are flagged as such via provenanceNote — treat
#    them as generally-informative, not as an authoritative LSPU
#    program specification.
#  - All programs are 4-year programs (programDurationYears 4), per
#    user confirmation.
#
#  REVISION 2: Admission cutoffs are now grounded in the official
#  "LSPU Admission Guidelines for the 1st Semester of AY 2026-2027"
#  (Office of the Guidance and Counseling, LSPU-LB), Annex A. This
#  confirmed all previously user-supplied GWA values and added the
#  one that had been missing (Bachelor of Physical Education = 90).
#  It also surfaced information not in the earlier Program Offers
#  list this file was originally built from:
#  - A College of Engineering offering Bachelor of Science in
#    Mechanical Engineering (GWA 87) has been added, flagged with
#    sourceDataGap since it wasn't part of the original program list.
#  - Two colleges are named differently in Annex A than in the
#    original Program Offers document ("College of Computer Studies"
#    vs. "College of Computer Science"; "College of Hospitality
#    Management and Tourism" vs. "College of International
#    Hospitality and Tourism"). The original names were kept and the
#    discrepancy flagged via sourceDataGap rather than guessing which
#    is current.
#  - Annex A states two college-wide admission conditions not
#    previously captured, now attached to the relevant programs'
#    AdmissionRequirement via admissionRequirementNote: CTE requires
#    no grade lower than 85 in English/Math/Science, and CCS gives
#    priority to STEM/ICT strand applicants.
#  - Annex A's Documentary Requirements and Admission Process (steps,
#    exam, interview, medical exam, enrolment) are NOT included here
#    since they describe a process/procedure rather than program
#    information — that content belongs under Pillar 2 (Admission &
#    Transaction Procedures).
#
#  REVISION 3 (this batch): Per user correction, LSPU-LB does not
#  actually offer a Bachelor of Science in Mechanical Engineering.
#  The College of Engineering, Degree_BSME, Prog_BSME, AdmReq_BSME,
#  and the two job outcomes / four skills that existed only for that
#  program have all been REMOVED — Annex A's inclusion of BSME is
#  treated as inapplicable to this campus.
#  - Added a CMO class plus hasLegalBasis/isLegalBasisFor properties
#    so each Program records the CHED Memorandum Order (CMO) that is
#    its national regulatory basis, gathered from the respective CMO
#    per the user's supplied list of 11. Programs that share one
#    Degree (the five BSEd majors; BSIT's three majors; BSTM/BSHM
#    under CMO 62) point to the same CMO individual.
#  - Three Degrees the user's CMO list did not cover (Bachelor of
#    Physical Education, Bachelor of Technology and Livelihood
#    Education, Bachelor of Technical-Vocational Teacher Education)
#    are sourced from CMO No. 80, 78, and 79 (all s. 2017)
#    respectively, rather than left blank. The CMO *numbers* are
#    corroborated across multiple independent sources; the cmoTitle
#    *wording* for these three is reconstructed from the standard
#    CHED PSG naming pattern, not copied from the primary CMO PDF —
#    each is flagged via sourceDataGap accordingly, and this flag is
#    intentionally being KEPT (not resolved) in this revision.
#  - Added boardProgram/licensureExamination so each Program records
#    whether its graduates sit a PRC board/licensure exam and, if so,
#    which one. Based on general current knowledge of PRC-regulated
#    professions in the Philippines, not an official LSPU document.
#  - Resolved the CCS/CIHT naming sourceDataGap from Revision 2 using
#    Annex A — the same document already treated as authoritative
#    elsewhere in this file: collegeName is now "College of Computer
#    Studies" and "College of Hospitality Management and Tourism"
#    respectively. The earlier Program-Offers-based names are kept in
#    the sourceDataGap note for continuity, not as open questions.
#  - Added a ProgramEducationalObjective class, attached per-CMO (via
#    hasProgramObjective), since a CMO's PSG is what actually defines
#    a program's educational objectives nationally, and several LSPU
#    programs share one CMO. These are general reconstructions of the
#    kind of objectives a CHED PSG for that field typically states,
#    NOT copied from any specific CMO's official PEO text (which this
#    file does not have access to) — flagged accordingly at the top
#    of that section rather than repeated per individual.
#################################################################

<http://lspu.edu.ph/ontology/program> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "LSPU-LB Program Information Ontology" ;
    rdfs:comment "Domain ontology for a student-facing RAG knowledge graph covering LSPU-LB's academic program offerings: colleges, degrees, majors, programs, admission requirements, each program's CMO regulatory basis, board/licensure status, general program educational objectives, generally-known skills developed, and career/job outcomes." .

#################################################################
#  CLASSES
#################################################################

lspuprog:College a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "College" ;
    rdfs:comment "An academic college of LSPU-LB (e.g. College of Computer Science) that houses one or more degree programs." .

lspuprog:Degree a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Degree" ;
    rdfs:comment "A base degree conferred by the university, independent of major/specialization (e.g. Bachelor of Science in Business Administration)." .

lspuprog:Major a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Major/Specialization" ;
    rdfs:comment "A named specialization track within a Degree (e.g. Marketing Management, Intelligent Systems). Some degrees have no major (e.g. BS Psychology, Bachelor of Physical Education, Bachelor of Elementary Education)." .

lspuprog:Program a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Program" ;
    rdfs:comment "A specific, enrollable degree+major combination offered by a College (e.g. 'BSBA - Major in Marketing Management'). This is the unit a student actually applies to and enrolls in." .

lspuprog:AdmissionRequirement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Admission Requirement" ;
    rdfs:comment "A program-specific entry requirement: the minimum general weighted average (GWA) needed to apply, per the 2026 LSPU-LB admission grade requirements supplied by the user." .

lspuprog:Skill a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Skill" ;
    rdfs:comment "A competency or capability a program is generally known to develop in students. Traceable via the parent Program's hasLegalBasis: each Skill reflects the kind of competency that Program's CMO/PSG typically specifies for that field, not a verbatim quote of the CMO's own competency list." .

lspuprog:JobOutcome a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Job/Career Outcome" ;
    rdfs:comment "A career path, job title, or professional track a program's graduates are generally known to pursue." .

lspuprog:CMO a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CHED Memorandum Order (CMO)" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Commission on Higher Education (CHED) Memorandum Order establishing the national Policies, Standards, and Guidelines (PSG) for a degree program. Recorded here as each Program's regulatory basis, gathered from the respective CMO rather than an LSPU-specific curriculum document." .

lspuprog:ProgramEducationalObjective a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Program Educational Objective (PEO)" ;
    rdfs:comment "A broad statement of what a program's graduates are expected to have attained a few years into their careers, as this kind of statement is typically defined at the national CMO/PSG level (see the REGULATORY BASIS section header for provenance)." .

#################################################################
#  OBJECT PROPERTIES
#################################################################

lspuprog:offeredByCollege a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range lspuprog:College ;
    rdfs:label "offeredByCollege" .

lspuprog:hasProgram a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf lspuprog:offeredByCollege ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:College ; rdfs:range lspuprog:Program ;
    rdfs:label "hasProgram" .

lspuprog:hasDegree a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range lspuprog:Degree ;
    rdfs:label "hasDegree" .

lspuprog:hasMajor a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range lspuprog:Major ;
    rdfs:label "hasMajor" ;
    rdfs:comment "Omitted for programs with no formal major (e.g. BS Psychology, Bachelor of Physical Education, Bachelor of Elementary Education)." .

lspuprog:teachesSkill a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range lspuprog:Skill ;
    rdfs:label "teachesSkill" .

lspuprog:preparesForOutcome a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range lspuprog:JobOutcome ;
    rdfs:label "preparesForOutcome" .

lspuprog:requiresSkill a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:JobOutcome ; rdfs:range lspuprog:Skill ;
    rdfs:label "requiresSkill" .

lspuprog:hasAdmissionRequirement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range lspuprog:AdmissionRequirement ;
    rdfs:label "hasAdmissionRequirement" .

lspuprog:hasLegalBasis a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range lspuprog:CMO ;
    rdfs:label "hasLegalBasis" ;
    rdfs:comment "Links a Program to the CHED Memorandum Order (CMO) that establishes its national policies, standards, and guidelines." .

lspuprog:isLegalBasisFor a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf lspuprog:hasLegalBasis ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:CMO ; rdfs:range lspuprog:Program ;
    rdfs:label "isLegalBasisFor" .

lspuprog:hasProgramObjective a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:CMO ; rdfs:range lspuprog:ProgramEducationalObjective ;
    rdfs:label "hasProgramObjective" ;
    rdfs:comment "Links a CMO to a general Program Educational Objective typical of that field's PSG. A Program inherits these via hasLegalBasis." .

lspuprog:isObjectiveOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf lspuprog:hasProgramObjective ;
    rdfs:domain lspuprog:ProgramEducationalObjective ; rdfs:range lspuprog:CMO ;
    rdfs:label "isObjectiveOf" .

#################################################################
#  DATA PROPERTIES
#################################################################

lspuprog:collegeName a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:College ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:College ; rdfs:range xsd:string .

lspuprog:degreeName a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Degree ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Degree ; rdfs:range xsd:string .

lspuprog:majorName a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Major ; rdfs:range xsd:string .

lspuprog:programName a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
lspuprog:programDurationYears a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range xsd:integer .
lspuprog:programOverview a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Short program description. Traceable via the Program's hasLegalBasis: it summarizes the kind of scope/content that Program's CMO/PSG typically covers for that field, based on general publicly-available knowledge of this degree type in the Philippine CHED context — not a verbatim quote of the CMO's own text, and not sourced from an official LSPU curriculum document." .

lspuprog:sourceDocument a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Filename or origin of the data this instance was extracted from, for RAG provenance tracking." .
lspuprog:sourceDataGap a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Notes a confirmed inconsistency or missing value in the source data (not fabricated to fill the gap)." .

lspuprog:minimumGeneralWeightedAverage a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:AdmissionRequirement ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:comment "Minimum general weighted average (GWA) required to apply, per the 2026 LSPU-LB admission grade requirements supplied by the user." .
lspuprog:admissionRequirementNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:AdmissionRequirement ; rdfs:range xsd:string .

lspuprog:skillName a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Skill ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
lspuprog:skillDescription a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Skill ; rdfs:range xsd:string .

lspuprog:jobOutcomeName a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:JobOutcome ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
lspuprog:jobOutcomeDescription a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:JobOutcome ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
lspuprog:provenanceNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:JobOutcome ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Notes that this outcome is drawn from general/publicly available knowledge about the field rather than an official LSPU program specification. Traceable via the parent Program's hasLegalBasis: it reflects the kind of career/job outcome that Program's CMO/PSG typically names for graduates of that field, not a verbatim quote of the CMO's own text — verify against the primary CMO if the RAG app needs to state it authoritatively." .

lspuprog:cmoNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:CMO ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "The CMO's series number as officially cited, preserving any leading zero (e.g. '05', '25')." .
lspuprog:cmoSeriesYear a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:CMO ; rdfs:range xsd:integer .
lspuprog:cmoCitation a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:CMO ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Precomposed short citation, e.g. 'CMO No. 25, s. 2015'." .
lspuprog:cmoTitle a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:CMO ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Official title of the CMO's Policies, Standards, and Guidelines (PSG). May name sister programs (e.g. BSIS) that this CMO also covers nationally but that LSPU-LB does not offer." .

lspuprog:boardProgram a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether graduates of this program sit a PRC (Professional Regulation Commission) board/licensure examination to practice the profession. Based on general current knowledge of Philippine PRC-regulated professions, not an official LSPU document; verify before stating authoritatively." .
lspuprog:licensureExamination a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:Program ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the PRC board/licensure examination this program's graduates are eligible to take. Present only when boardProgram is true." .

lspuprog:peoText a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain lspuprog:ProgramEducationalObjective ; rdfs:range xsd:string .

#################################################################
#  COLLEGES  (source: Program Offers document)
#################################################################

lspuprog:CAS  a lspuprog:College ; lspuprog:collegeName "College of Arts and Sciences" ; lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation "CAS" .
lspuprog:CBAA a lspuprog:College ; lspuprog:collegeName "College of Business Administration and Accountancy" ; lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation "CBAA" .
lspuprog:CCS  a lspuprog:College ; lspuprog:collegeName "College of Computer Studies" ; lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation "CCS" ;
    lspuprog:sourceDataGap "Resolved: the earlier Program Offers document named this college 'College of Computer Science'; the official LSPU Admission Guidelines (1st Sem AY 2026-2027), Annex A — treated as the current authority elsewhere in this file (e.g. GWA values) — names it 'College of Computer Studies', now used here. 'College of Computer Science' is kept only as a historical alternate name." .
lspuprog:CCJE a lspuprog:College ; lspuprog:collegeName "College of Criminal Justice Education" ; lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation "CCJE" .
lspuprog:CF   a lspuprog:College ; lspuprog:collegeName "College of Fisheries" ; lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation "CF" .
lspuprog:CFND a lspuprog:College ; lspuprog:collegeName "College of Food Nutrition and Dietetics" ; lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation "CFND" .
lspuprog:CIHT a lspuprog:College ; lspuprog:collegeName "College of Hospitality Management and Tourism" ; lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation "CIHT" ;
    lspuprog:sourceDataGap "Resolved: the earlier Program Offers document named this college 'College of International Hospitality and Tourism'; the official LSPU Admission Guidelines (1st Sem AY 2026-2027), Annex A — treated as the current authority elsewhere in this file (e.g. GWA values) — names it 'College of Hospitality Management and Tourism', now used here. 'College of International Hospitality and Tourism' is kept only as a historical alternate name." .
lspuprog:CTE  a lspuprog:College ; lspuprog:collegeName "College of Teacher Education" ; lspuprog:collegeAbbreviation "CTE" .

#################################################################
#  DEGREES & MAJORS
#################################################################

lspuprog:Degree_BSPsychology a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Psychology" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BS Psychology" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSAccountancy a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Accountancy" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSA" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSBA a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Business Administration" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSBA" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSIT a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Information Technology" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSIT" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSCS a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Computer Science" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSCS" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSCriminology a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Criminology" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSCrim" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSFisheries a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Fisheries" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSF" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSFoodTechnology a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Food Technology" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSFT" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSNutritionDietetics a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Nutrition and Dietetics" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSND" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSTourismManagement a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Tourism Management" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSTM" .
lspuprog:Degree_BSHospitalityManagement a lspuprog:Degree ; lspuprog:degreeName "Bachelor of Science in Hospitality Management" ; lspuprog:degreeAbbreviation "BSHM" .
